{"parentUuid":"8668f2d5-453e-40b9-9343-b4143732380a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8/crates/core/tests/relevance_props_type.rs","snippet":"1\t#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic)]\n2\t//! The lane facts the props-type evidence of ADR 0028 (slice T2, `relevance::props_type::members`) reads, pinned at\n3\t//! the public output: the evidence itself is crate-private and tested beside it. A member the props type redeclares is\n4\t//! a listed prop and no member of its base's collapsed layer (a collapsed layer never holds a listed name, though the\n5\t//! structural own-vs-inherited split still marks it overriding); a `Pick`'s keys are listed with their base as `parent`; an `Omit`'s key is in neither; and a\n6\t//! collapsed layer names its members only, so a required member in it is known by name alone in either lane.\n7\t\n8\tuse caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::{CollapseInheritedProps, HtmlAttributeMode, PipelineOptions, extract};\n9\tuse caliper_docgen_core::types::{ComponentEntry, ExtractionOutput};\n10\tuse std::sync::OnceLock;\n11\t\n12\tuse camino::Utf8PathBuf;\n13\tuse tempfile::TempDir;"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1e661456-fb5c-405b-9e73-3c9c51afa993","timestamp":"2026-11-16T05:27:33.872Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8/crates/core/tests/relevance_props_type.rs changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic)]\n2\t//! The lane facts the props-type evidence of ADR 0028 (slice T2, `relevance::props_type::members`) reads, pinned at\n3\t//! the public output: the evidence itself is crate-private and tested beside it. A member the props type redeclares is\n4\t//! a listed prop and no member of its base's collapsed layer (a collapsed layer never holds a listed name, though the\n5\t//! structural own-vs-inherited split still marks it overriding); a `Pick`'s keys are listed with their base as `parent`; an `Omit`'s key is in neither; and a\n6\t//! collapsed layer names its members only, so a required member in it is known by name alone in either lane.\n7\t\n8\tuse caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::{CollapseInheritedProps, HtmlAttributeMode, PipelineOptions, extract};\n9\tuse caliper_docgen_core::types::{ComponentEntry, ExtractionOutput};\n10\tuse std::sync::OnceLock;\n11\t\n12\tuse camino::Utf8PathBuf;\n13\tuse tempfile::TempDir;\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix-480-disc","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
