{"parentUuid":"2325315c-77cd-4bac-b0a5-8cb73b1a6cd6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch65gzqjxZEYjceCVu8zm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PajJxMMT8DRqjFYgRUwXXz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"281: lazy delta reports changed relevance of retained answers","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Fix one finding on change 281 (PR 483, branch `feat/relevance-output`, trail 405). `git fetch origin` (if fetch is blocked, use the existing origin refs); start from `origin/feat/relevance-output`; local branch `fix/lazy-delta-used`; commit locally; I push. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md (incl. Pre-push gate), then `entire trail finding show 01M7HDCRWP08 --branch feat/relevance-output --repo gh/orin-dx/caliper --project gh/orin-dx` and crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs (~290-310 `next_lazy`, ~380-390 `lazy_delta`, ~654-656), revision.rs (the eager path already reports components whose layers/`used` changed through call sites: reuse that rule, one owner), relevance/mod.rs `apply`. The finding: after a lazy session resolves `Button`, editing only a CONSUMER's JSX can change Button's `used` list without it appearing in `updated_keys`, because `next_lazy` keeps the retained resolution without marking it touched and `lazy_delta` reports only touched names; clients that rely on update notifications keep stale relevance data. Fix: for retained lazy answers, compare the relevance-bearing result (the `used` lists/relevance evidence) against the new revision's call-site evidence and include the affected keys in the delta, using the same comparison the eager path uses (do not write a second rule). Known context: an earlier parked branch tried this (commit 7137bf80, local only, in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a518d0c89389edba6; `git log` may show it): read it for ideas, do not copy blindly. Tests first (fail on base) in the watch/lazy model test (crates/core/tests/relevance_watch_model.rs): add an edit kind 'edit only a consumer's JSX' (add/remove `<Button className>` in another file) after a lazy resolution, and assert the lazy delta's updated keys include Button when its `used` changed and do NOT include unaffected components; also an import-only edit kind (consumer's import changes which tag is Button). Mutation proof: removing your comparison makes the model fail. Gates (targeted): `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` in the worktree first; `just lint doc-check machete typos`; nextest `-p caliper-docgen-core -p caliper-docgen-semantic`; `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in the worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release); report watch edit refresh time before/after on gate-large if cheap (skip if not). Then `/code-review low` once and AWAIT its output; fix only real bugs. Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 60 tool calls. Final message at most 50 words: branch, SHA, exit codes, mutation result."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1153,"cache_read_input_tokens":637287,"output_tokens":2517,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1153,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":637287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1153},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_ma