{"parentUuid":"240ff27e-5366-49f6-89aa-109de86149a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch66TGkw3pey5MwSujhRZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Change 281 (#483) is fixed and pushed as be358fd4, and its finding is resolved. Both open changes with findings, 278 and 281, now have none.\n\n**The 281 fix.** Retained lazy answers are now compared with the eager path's `layers_differ` rule. When a consumer's JSX changes a component's relevance, that component is reported in the lazy delta's updated keys. It's one rule with one owner.\n\n**Evidence (worker's report)**\n- The new watch and lazy model test, with a consumer-JSX-only edit, fails on the base. Removing the comparison, in two different ways, makes it fail, so the check is real.\n- Lint, doc-check, machete, typos, nextest on core and semantic, and the checker lane all exit 0.\n- `/code-review low` found no findings. The watch refresh timing was skipped.\n\n**State:** #483 and #480 both show BLOCKED (awaiting approval), none DIRTY, no open findings on either. The only other open PR is #487, the Wisp v5 chore.\n\n**Merge order:** #480 (change 278), then #483 (change 281). CI is the remaining check; I haven't run the full gates myself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":656301,"output_tokens":386,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":656301,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transform